cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AnestheSIM, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "AnestheSIM: an open, extensible patient simulator for closed-loop anesthesia driven by VitalDB records"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Isabela
    family-names: Birs
    email: isabela.birs@aut.utcluj.ro
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-13
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/izabirs/AnestheSIM"
abstract: >-
  AnestheSIM is an open MATLAB/Simulink patient simulator for closed-loop
  anesthesia research and teaching, in which acquisition from the VitalDB open
  surgical database is a native, extensible layer. Recorded or designed pump
  rates and end-tidal gas concentrations drive covariate pharmacokinetic
  models of propofol, remifentanil and norepinephrine, three interchangeable
  BIS interaction models, an intravenous-inhalational model for sevoflurane
  and desflurane, and MAP/HR models, all with published parameters. The
  release includes cohort search, automatic inhaled-agent resolution, alarms,
  synthetic patients, unit tests and the scripts that validate the simulator
  on VitalDB records.
keywords:
  - anesthesia
  - patient simulator
  - closed-loop control
  - pharmacokinetics
  - pharmacodynamics
  - VitalDB
  - MATLAB
  - Simulink
  - education
